              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The URL you provided, **[www.profedcreditunion.com](https://profedcu.org)**, belongs to **ProFed Federal Credit Union** (commonly known as ProFed). \n\nHere is an overview of what ProFed Credit Union is, who can join, and the services they provide:\n\n### **About ProFed Credit Union**\nProFed is a community-chartered, member-owned financial cooperative founded in 1933. It is headquartered in **Fort Wayne, Indiana**, and serves communities across northeast Indiana. \n\n### **Who Can Join? (Eligibility)**\nBecause ProFed is a community-chartered credit union, membership is open to anyone who **lives, works, worships, volunteers, or regularly conducts business** in any of the following nine northeast Indiana counties:\n* Adams\n* Allen\n* DeKalb\n* Huntington\n* LaGrange\n* Noble\n* Steuben\n* Wells\n* Whitley\n\n### **Financial Services Offered**\nProFed provides personal and business banking products, including:\n* **Savings & Checking Accounts:** High-yield savings, checking accounts with debit cards, and certificates of deposit (CDs).\n* **Loans:** Auto loans, personal loans, and recreational vehicle loans.\n* **Mortgages:** Home purchases, refinancing, and home equity lines of credit (HELOC).\n* **Credit Cards:** Visa\u00ae Rewards and other credit card options.\n* **Digital Banking:** A mobile app (\"ProFed Digital Banking\") for online transfers, mobile check deposit, bill pay, and managing card controls.\n\n### **Key Branch & Contact Information**\n* **Official Website:** [profedcu.org](https://profedcu.org) (The URL you entered automatically redirects to their main website).\n* **Main Headquarters:** 1710 Saint Joe River Dr., Fort Wayne, IN 46805.\n* **Phone Number:** \n  * Main: 260-483-0514\n  * Toll-Free: 800-752-4613\n* **Locations:** ProFed has 13 physical branch locations across northeast Indiana, many of which feature 24/7 ATMs and drive-up Interactive Video Tellers (ITMs).\n\n*Are you looking for specific help with your ProFed account, routing numbers, or finding a branch near you? Let me know!*",
